Guard four more event families that fire on per-tick or per-spawn paths.

EntityInsideBlockEvent - 24 byte-identical call sites across world/level/block. Each builds a
CraftBlock and an event every time an entity is inside one of those blocks, which for bubble
columns, cobwebs, berry bushes, fire, portals and pressure plates is every tick that entity stays
there. Veto-only, so with no listener it can never return early.

EntityEffectTickEvent - fires on every effect application tick for every entity carrying an
effect, building a CraftEntity handle and converting the potion type each time. Veto-only.

ServerTickStartEvent / ServerTickEndEvent - two allocations every tick, forever, on servers that
mostly have no listener for either.

PreCreatureSpawnEvent (EntityType#spawn), PreSpawnerSpawnEvent (BaseSpawner#serverTick) and
PhantomPreSpawnEvent - each builds two or three Craft conversions plus an event per spawn attempt.
All three are veto-only, and shouldAbortSpawn() is only read when the event was cancelled, which
cannot happen with nothing listening.

Worth recording: Leaf already guards the hottest PreCreatureSpawnEvent site itself, in
NaturalSpawner#isValidSpawnPostitionForType, with the comment "Skip PreCreatureSpawnEvent if no
listeners". These are the sites upstream did not cover, and upstream doing the same thing in the
same way is good evidence the pattern is sound rather than a private trick.
